IMPORTANT

Because the large files were already committed, they still exist in Git history.

Check .git size:

Shell
du -sh .git

If it's still huge (hundreds of MB), easiest fix for a learning project:

Reinitialize Git
Shell
rm -rf .git
 
git init
 

Then:

Shell
git add .
 
git commit -m "Initial Commit"

Add remote:

Shell
git remote add origin https://github.com/hyarelgits/Future-Agentic-Ai.git

Push:

Shell
git branch -M main
 
git push -u origin main
Recommended for Your Project

Since this is a training project and not production:

Shell
rm -rf .git
 
git init
 
nano .gitignore

(add exclusions)

Then:

Shell
git add .
 
git commit -m "Initial Commit"
 
git push -u origin main
 

This is faster than cleaning the old Git history and will completely remove the oversized files from the repository history.

